{"name":"Pumpkin Soup","hex":"#e17701","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pumpkin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domesticated plant, in species Cucurbita pepo, similar in growth pattern, foliage, flower, and fruit to the squash or melon.","The round yellow or orange fruit of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pumpkin"},{"term":"soup","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various dishes commonly made by combining liquids, such as water or stock, with other ingredients, such as meat and vegetables, that contribute the food value, flavor, and texture.","A serving of such a dish, typically in a bowl."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feed: to provide with soup or a meal.","To develop (film) in a (chemical) developing solution."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soup"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pumpkin Soup","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pumpkin Soup\" is a song by Kate Nash that is featured on her fourth single, the third to be lifted from her debut album Made of Bricks. It was released on 17 December 2007, making it a contender for the Christmas number one and entered the charts at number 58 on the UK Singles Chart based on downloads only, then reached number 40 with a physical release the following week. It reached a peak of number 23 on 6 January, equalling the peak of previous single \"Mouthwash\". The song spent total 10 weeks on the UK Singles Chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b8/Kate_Nash_-_Pumpkin_Soup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumpkin_Soup","wikidata":"Q368439"},{"title":"Pumpkin soup","blocks":[{"text":"Pumpkin soup is a usually 'bound' (thick) soup made from a purée of pumpkin. It is made by combining the meat of a blended pumpkin with broth or stock. It can be served hot or cold, and is a common Thanksgiving dish in the United States. Various versions of the dish are known in many European countries, the United States and other areas of North America, in Asia and in Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/K%C3%BCrbissuppe_mit_Kern%C3%B6l.JPG/330px-K%C3%BCrbissuppe_mit_Kern%C3%B6l.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumpkin_soup","wikidata":"Q1797271"},{"title":"Pumpkin","blocks":[{"text":"A pumpkin is a cultivated winter squash in the genus Cucurbita. The term is most commonly applied to round, orange-colored squash varieties, but does not possess a scientific definition. It may be used in reference to many different squashes of varied appearance and belonging to multiple species in the Cucurbita genus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/FrenchMarketPumpkinsB.jpg/330px-FrenchMarketPumpkinsB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumpkin","wikidata":"Q165308"},{"title":"Soup","blocks":[{"text":"Soup is a primarily liquid food, generally served warm or hot – though it is sometimes served chilled – made by cooking or otherwise combining meat or vegetables with stock, milk, or water. According to The Oxford Companion to Food, soup is the main generic term for liquid savoury dishes; others include broth, bisque, consommé, potage and many more."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Asparagus_soup_%28spargelsuppe%29.jpg/330px-Asparagus_soup_%28spargelsuppe%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soup","wikidata":"Q41415"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Crema_de_calabaza.JPG/250px-Crema_de_calabaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Crema_de_calabaza.JPG/330px-Crema_de_calabaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Crema_de_calabaza.JPG/250px-Crema_de_calabaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrema_de_calabaza.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Cucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG/250px-Cucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Cucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG/500px-Cucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Cucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG/250px-Cucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACucurbita_maxima_Zapallo_Plomo_semiller%C3%ADa_Costanzi_-_2014_08_01_-_squash_A_soup_4.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Harefield%2C_Harefield%2C_London_%283363509227%29.jpg/250px-Harefield%2C_Harefield%2C_London_%283363509227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Harefield%2C_Harefield%2C_London_%283363509227%29.jpg/500px-Harefield%2C_Harefield%2C_London_%283363509227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thu